+## Separately authorized invalidated first-turn recovery
+
+After a BLOCKED first turn has ended, a later turn in that same reserved context
+cannot supply admissible review evidence. Preserve its output and reservation.
+Do not start B from it, release its identity, or loosen `--recover-interrupted`.
+
+For the specifically authorized three-attempt chain (terminal → no-output
+interruption → failed-first-turn with resumed diagnostic output), the
+orchestrator may use `--reset --fresh-review-contract=<path>` (PowerShell:
+`-Reset -FreshReviewContract <path>`) to open only the next attempt, round 1.
+The contract uses `spec-fresh-review-recovery/v1` as defined by the read-only
+`scripts/fresh-review-recovery.py`: pin current Pending input hashes, every
+required prior evidence file, both original invocation manifests, and the
+complete host transcript identifying the failed and resumed turns. Retain that
+immutable contract as the provenance named by the new precheck's
+`fresh_review_contract_sha256`. This opt-in route alone requires Python 3.
+The precheck validates the terminal contract and both persisted reservations,
+then repeats all admission checks under the transition lock. It does not reserve
+an identity or produce a review verdict.
